        {
          "id": "SP_MAGNIPELTA_MYCOPHAGA_PILSBRY_1953",
          "name": "Magnipelta mycophaga Pilsbry, 1953",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "Magnum mantleslug",
          "lineage": "Magnipelta",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Light tan body and mantle with black spots; broad mantle covering most of dorsum with a black longitudinal stripe on either side; pneumostome posterior to middle of mantle (Forsyth 2004); keel present; no caudal mucus pore; sole is sometimes 3-part, sometimes not (Leonard et al. 2011).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Epiphallus present; buccal and tentacular retractors joined behind diaphragm (Leonard et al. 2011).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:2294052",
          "authorship": "Pilsbry",
