        {
          "id": "SP_HESPERARION_MARIAE_BRANSON_1991",
          "name": "Hesperarion mariae Branson, 1991",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Hesperarion",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Light red-gray body and mantle; lighter sides; darker head and neck; large, irregular black spots and marks on mantle; little black spots that may form lines along skin grooves; mantle forms a hump over internal shell; light and dark stripes on foot fringe; large, downward-bent caudal mucus pit; slightly 3-part, white sole (Branson 1991; Roth 2004).</p><p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\"> </p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Asymmetric internal shell; cylindrical penis with a large conical verge in the apex; large, thin-walled dart sac with one long, curved dart in the atrium; oviduct significantly longer than penis (Branson 1991; Roth 2004).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:2294073",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "1e78c432-9e34-58f-83f-a876792ff1be8b",
          "sourceIds": {
            "col": [
              "7RNY2"
            ],
            "itis": [
              "567686"
            ]
          },
          "authorityIds": "col:7RNY2,itis:567686"
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_HESPERARION_NIGER",
          "name": "Hesperarion niger",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "Black westernslug",
          "lineage": "Hesperarion",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Black brown to red gray body and mantle, lighter on sides; small black spots on body, forming lines along mucus grooves; tan to gray foot fringe with black stripes; white to pale tan sole, sometimes with black spots on side portions; caudal mucus pore present (Roth 2004). </p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Internal shell asymmetric; cylindrical penis with narrow base, and retractor and epiphallus at apex; small conical verge in apex of penis; epiphallus of constant width; three large pilasters in atrium; appendix on base or dart sac of atrium; dart sac of atrium contains multiple curved darts (Roth 2004).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:2294074",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "f741fbf5-06c6-5f3-90d-cc595863cf4a23",
          "sourceIds": {
            "col": [
              "7RNY3"
            ],
            "itis": [
              "77098"
            ],
            "checklistbank": [
              "urn:lsid:marinespecies.org:taxname:1352269"
            ]
          },
          "authorityIds": "checklistbank:urn:lsid:marinespecies.org:taxname:1352269,col:7RNY3,itis:77098",
          "authorship": "(J. G. Cooper, 1872)"
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_HESPERARION_PLUMBEUS_B_ROTH_2004",
          "name": "Hesperarion plumbeus B.Roth, 2004",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Hesperarion",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Mantle ~30% of body length; unicolor gray body, with lighter sides and neck and slight dark mottling on mantle; skin grooves slightly darkened; keel present; foot fringe light tan to gray, without strong stripes; light tan sole; caudal mucus pore present (Roth 2004).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Short penis, broader toward apex, and with internal teardrop-shaped verge; penial retractor on first bend of epiphallus; appendix next to free oviduct on atrium; long spermatheca duct, broader for first half of length than the second half; small, acorn-shaped spermatheca (Roth 2004).</p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Differs from <em>H. niger</em>, because penis is shorter and has a teardrop-shaped rather than conical verge (Roth 2004). .</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:9881754",
          "authorship": "B.Roth",
          "yearPublished": "2004",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "16d02598-6f1f-534-bcd-99f1633fae308e",
          "sourceIds": {
            "col": [
              "7RNY4"
            ]
          },
          "authorityIds": "col:7RNY4"
        },
