        {
          "id": "SP_ARIOLIMAX_DOLICHOPHALLUS_MEAD_1943",
          "name": "Ariolimax dolichophallus Mead, 1943",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "Slender banana slug",
          "lineage": "Ariolimax",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">External: Slender, medium-sized <em>Ariolimax</em>; bright yellow, without spots (Harper 1988); slightly darker longitudinal grooves in skin; 3-part sole, wider than dorsum, and with side sections similar in color or slightly darker than middle section (Mead 1943).</p><p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\"> </p> <p style=\"margin: 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px 0.0px; font: 14.0px Helvetica;\">Internal: Penis tubular, 60-110 mm long fully extended, with a flagellum-like apical section 2-4x the length of the basal thick portion; vas deferens follows along penis flagellum and joins apex; penis retractor attached at 1/4 to 1/3 from its base; short, curved vagina with a thin-walled and a thick-walled portion; spermatheca attached to vagina above the retentor muscles; short oviduct; short atrium (Mead 1943).</p>",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
